.TH ASTERCTL-QUERY 1 "2026-09-24" "Aster" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
asterctl-query \- query Events stored on an Aster node
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY asterctl
.RI [ GLOBAL-OPTIONS ]
.B query
.RI [ QUERY-OPTIONS ]
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
Query locally stored Events through a running Aster agent.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-topic " TOPIC"
Optional. Filter by exact Event topic.
.TP
.BI \-\-scope " SCOPE"
Optional. Filter by exact Event scope.
Use a trailing '/*' to include this scope and all sub-scopes.
Example: \%'mission/team/*'.
.TP
.BI \-\-publisher " ID"
Filter by publisher identity.
ID is a Base64-encoded 32-byte node identity.
.TP
.BI \-\-logical\-key " KEY"
Optional. Filter by exact logical key supplied as UTF-8 text.
.TP
.BI \-\-limit " NUMBER"
Limit the number of Events to display.
The number of matching Events returned may be smaller.
.IP
Default: unlimited.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Query succeeded, including an empty result.
.TP
.B 1
Authentication, RPC, or input/output failure.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line arguments.
.SH EXAMPLES
Query Events:
.PP
.nf
.RS
asterctl \-\-token\-file ./client.token query
.RE
.fi
.PP
Filter by topic and scope:
.PP
.nf
.RS
asterctl \-\-token\-file ./client.token query \e
    \-\-topic chat.events \e
    \-\-scope mission/team/alpha
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR asterctl (1),
.BR asterctl-publish (1)
